{
  "uid": "dcms-retention",
  "title": "Retention & disk",
  "description": "Telemetry store sizes against their budgets, and what to do when one overruns.",
  "tags": [
    "dcms",
    "ops",
    "retention"
  ],
  "timezone": "browser",
  "schemaVersion": 39,
  "version": 1,
  "editable": true,
  "graphTooltip": 1,
  "refresh": "5m",
  "time": {
    "from": "now-7d",
    "to": "now"
  },
  "timepicker": {},
  "templating": {
    "list": []
  },
  "annotations": {
    "list": [
      {
        "builtIn": 1,
        "datasource": {
          "type": "grafana",
          "uid": "-- Grafana --"
        },
        "enable": true,
        "hide": true,
        "iconColor": "rgba(0, 211, 255, 1)",
        "name": "Annotations & Alerts",
        "type": "dashboard"
      }
    ]
  },
  "panels": [
    {
      "id": 5,
      "type": "text",
      "title": "",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 12,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "**The telemetry budget: ~20 GB per environment.**\n\nThe caps below were sized against the 40 GB free on dev (vps1). dev and prod run separate stacks with separate disks, so prod enforces the same caps against its own headroom \u2014 raise them there rather than assuming the numbers still fit.\n\n| Store | Retention | Cap | Enforced by |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Prometheus | 30 d | 8 GB | `--storage.tsdb.retention.size` |\n| Loki | 30 d (90 d audit/security) | ~8 GB | `retention_period` + compactor |\n| Tempo | 7 d | ~4 GB | `block_retention` |\n| Docker json logs | 3 \u00d7 50 MB per container | ~3 GB | the `x-logging` anchor |\n\nLoki has no size cap \u2014 that is not a Loki feature \u2014 so its budget is held by the retention period plus the ingestion-rate limits. If it overruns, the cause is almost always one service logging in a loop, not steady growth.\n\n**If Tempo is the one over budget**, the fix is already written and commented out: `infra/observability/alloy/config.alloy` ships tail sampling set to keep 100%, with the errors-and-slow-plus-10%-baseline policies below it. Uncomment those before shortening retention \u2014 a shorter window breaks the support workflow for everyone, while sampling only loses the uneventful traces."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 19,
      "type": "row",
      "title": "Budget: measured, not estimated",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 12
      },
      "collapsed": false,
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "id": 20,
      "type": "bargauge",
      "title": "Share of budget used, per store",
      "description": "The only panel on this dashboard that answers the question the budget is written to ask. Everything else here is an ingest rate, from which you can infer growth and cannot say whether 8/8/4 GB is being kept.\n\nMeasured against the six-hour PEAK, not the current size: these stores sawtooth (Alloy's WAL truncates, Prometheus compacts), and what the disk has to hold is the top. Budgets come from docs/adr/0008-observability.md as their own series, so a panel and a rule cannot disagree about them.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "dcms-prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 10,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 13
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "dcms-prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "dcms:store_disk_used_ratio",
          "legendFormat": "{{store}}"
        }
      ],
      "options": {
        "displayMode": "gradient",
        "orientation": "horizontal",
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "showUnfilled": true,
        "minVizWidth": 8,
        "minVizHeight": 16
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "percentunit",
          "min": 0,
          "max": 1.2,
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          },
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "orange",
                "value": 0.75
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 1.0
              }
            ]
          },
          "mappings": []
        },
        "overrides": []
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 21,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "On disk, per store",
      "description": "Prometheus self-reports its TSDB size. Loki and Tempo report theirs nowhere at all, which is why all three are measured from outside instead.\n\nThe sawtooth is normal: Alloy's remote-write WAL ramps and truncates every couple of hours, and Prometheus writes blocks then compacts them. The dashed lines are the budgets.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "dcms-prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 14,
        "x": 10,
        "y": 13
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "dcms-prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "dcms_store_disk_bytes",
          "legendFormat": "{{store}}"
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "dcms-prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "dcms_store_disk_budget_bytes",
          "legendFormat": "{{store}} budget"
        },
        {
          "refId": "C",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "dcms-prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "dcms:store_disk_peak_bytes",
          "legendFormat": "{{store}} peak/6h"
        }
      ],
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "right",
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull",
            "max"
          ],
          "showLegend": true
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "bytes",
          "min": 0,
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 8,
            "showPoints": "never",
            "spanNulls": true
          },
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
          },
          "mappings": [],
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": [
          {
            "matcher": {
              "id": "byRegexp",
              "options": ".* budget"
            },
            "properties": [
              {
                "id": "custom.lineStyle",
                "value": {
                  "fill": "dash",
                  "dash": [
                    8,
                    6
                  ]
                }
              },
              {
                "id": "custom.fillOpacity",
                "value": 0
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 22,
      "type": "table",
      "title": "Projected size at the end of the retention window",
      "description": "The six-hour peak plus the trend of the peaks over a day, carried to the store's own retention horizon \u2014 30 days for Prometheus and Loki, 7 for Tempo.\n\nThis is the number to compare against the budget, not the current size: a store two weeks into a thirty-day window looks perfectly healthy right up until it isn't, and by the time the plain over-budget alert fires there is nothing left to do but delete data.\n\nThe trend is taken over peaks rather than through the raw series because these stores sawtooth \u2014 a slope fitted to the raw series measures whichever edge it spans. Meaningless for the first day after a deploy; the alert carries the same guard.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "dcms-prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 21
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "dcms-prometheus"
          },
          "format": "table",
          "instant": true,
          "expr": "dcms:store_disk_peak_bytes",
          "legendFormat": "{{store}}"
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "dcms-prometheus"
          },
          "format": "table",
          "instant": true,
          "expr": "dcms:store_disk_growth_bytes_per_second * 86400",
          "legendFormat": "{{store}}"
        },
        {
          "refId": "C",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "dcms-prometheus"
          },
          "format": "table",
          "instant": true,
          "expr": "dcms:store_disk_projected_bytes",
          "legendFormat": "{{store}}"
        },
        {
          "refId": "D",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "dcms-prometheus"
          },
          "format": "table",
          "instant": true,
          "expr": "dcms_store_disk_budget_bytes",
          "legendFormat": "{{store}}"
        }
      ],
      "transformations": [
        {
          "id": "joinByField",
          "options": {
            "byField": "store",
            "mode": "outer"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "organize",
          "options": {
            "excludeByName": {
              "Time": true,
              "Time 1": true,
              "Time 2": true,
              "Time 3": true,
              "Time 4": true,
              "job": true,
              "job 1": true,
              "job 2": true,
              "job 3": true,
              "job 4": true,
              "instance": true,
              "instance 1": true,
              "instance 2": true,
              "instance 3": true,
              "instance 4": true
            },
            "renameByName": {
              "store": "Store",
              "Value #A": "Peak (6h)",
              "Value #B": "Growth / day",
              "Value #C": "Projected at retention",
              "Value #D": "Budget"
            }
          }
        }
      ],
      "options": {
        "showHeader": true,
        "cellHeight": "sm",
        "footer": {
          "show": false,
          "reducer": [
            "sum"
          ],
          "countRows": false,
          "fields": ""
        }
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "bytes",
          "custom": {
            "align": "auto",
            "cellOptions": {
              "type": "auto"
            }
          },
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          },
          "mappings": [],
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "text",
                "value": null
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": [
          {
            "matcher": {
              "id": "byName",
              "options": "Store"
            },
            "properties": [
              {
                "id": "unit",
                "value": "string"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "matcher": {
              "id": "byName",
              "options": "Projected at retention"
            },
            "properties": [
              {
                "id": "custom.cellOptions",
                "value": {
                  "type": "color-background",
                  "mode": "gradient"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": "thresholds",
                "value": {
                  "mode": "absolute",
                  "steps": [
                    {
                      "color": "green",
                      "value": null
                    },
                    {
                      "color": "orange",
                      "value": 4000000000.0
                    },
                    {
                      "color": "red",
                      "value": 8000000000.0
                    }
                  ]
                }
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
